{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"IMPLEMENTED on branch fix/55bc-sidecar-prune (worktree rebar-wt-55bc, based on origin/main).\n\nHANDOFF VERIFIED ACCURATE against the real tree before editing. All three call sites were exactly where documented (plan_review/sidecar.py:89, code_review/sidecar.py:148, completion_sidecar.py:59) with the documented text, and both defect-asserting unit tests were at the documented lines.\n\nRED FIRST — captured, all three paths, through the real emit() path. New two-clone repros in tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py (reusing the existing two_clones fixture and following the 8185/be8a0c059 enrichment-drain prior art): bare remote + clones A/B sharing one tickets branch, base padded to the retention bound with REAL emitted payloads, both clones offline, one automatic emit each.\n\nPre-fix control merge of the shared base: rc=0. Post-emit merge, pre-fix:\n- test_plan_review_sidecar_emit_two_clone_union -> CONFLICT (rename/rename): <base>-REVIEW_RESULT.json renamed to 1785643613287151001-f2bde524-...-REVIEW_RESULT.json in HEAD and to 1785643613658129001-19c0b6fe-...-REVIEW_RESULT.json in the peer.\n- test_code_review_sidecar_emit_two_clone_union -> CONFLICT (rename/rename), same shape.\n- test_completion_sidecar_emit_two_clone_union -> CONFLICT (rename/rename), same shape.\n3 failed in 45.23s. The equal-length-neighbour trap from the RCA is handled by padding the base with real emit() payloads; the conflict reproduced on the first attempt, no spurious green.\n\nThe two inverted unit tests were also verified RED before the fix: test_code_review_emit_keeps_every_event_past_the_cap (assert 50 == 53) and test_code_review_emit_does_not_call_prune. 2 failed, 2 passed — the two direct-call prune() tests stayed green and untouched.\n\nFIX: removed the automatic prune() call from all three emit() paths. prune() itself is unchanged and still importable as an explicit operator-invoked op; docstrings now state the append-only contract and that prune must never be called from a write path. Post-fix: all 3 repros GREEN (68.11s), all 4 unit retention tests GREEN.\n\nMUTATION CHECK: re-added prune(target_ticket, ...) to code_review emit -> test_code_review_sidecar_emit_two_clone_union back to RED with the same rename/rename CONFLICT, and both inverted unit tests back to RED. Mutation removed; green restored.\n\nSIBLING SWEEP: grep for prune call sites in src/ now returns only the three def lines — zero automatic invocations remain.\n\nGATES: make lint exit 0 (ruff check + ruff format --check + dco + criteria vocab + zizmor + actionlint, exit code checked directly, not piped). make typecheck exit 0 (mypy, 407 files)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785644614801291001,"uuid":"7f8314bb-fd7e-4172-b043-8e816a802df6"}